      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "sdge:cc-dr-2026-06-01",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "sdge:cc-dr-2026-06-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing models the standard Schedule DR customer only: the Base Services Charge of $0.79343 per day, the flat EECC generation rate of $0.18274 per kWh, the eight UDC components, DWR-BC and WF-NBC, and the $0.10663 per kWh Baseline Adjustment Credit that produces the Tier 1 rate. Four published provisions are not represented. The DR-MB rate table on Sheet 2, whose total effective Medical Baseline rates are $0.31782 per kWh up to 130 percent of baseline and $0.40138 above it, with DWR-BC and WF-NBC not applying (note 3) and no Base Services Charge discount (note 6); no SDG&E Medical Baseline overlay exists in this corpus, so that customer class cannot be billed from the data at all. The Franchise Fee Differential of 5.78 percent applied to monthly billings for customers inside the corporate limits of the City of San Diego. The Direct Access and Community Choice Aggregation bill path of Special Condition 9.b, under which the EECC and DWR-BC components are credited back and the applicable Cost Responsibility Surcharge is added; the EECC that is modeled is the bundled rate, which per Special Condition 11 already embeds the Power Charge Indifference Adjustment. And the semi-annual California Climate Credit of $49.36 under Schedule GHG-ARR named in the applicability section. Separately, the two service tiers are bounded at a dimensionless 1.3 standing for 130 percent of the customer's allowance, so the Special Condition 3 allowance table itself (Basic Allowance 9.0, 10.4, 13.6 and 15.9 kWh per day in summer for the Coastal, Inland, Mountain and Desert zones and 9.2, 9.6, 12.9 and 10.9 in winter, with a separate All Electric set) is absent and a consumer must supply the customer's allowance to resolve the tier boundary. Two groups of provisions are out of scope rather than missing: the DR-LI (CARE) column and the DRAH and FERA Base Services Charges of $0.39688 per day are carried by separate overlay filings, and Special Conditions 1, 5, 6, 7 and 8 (load checks, standard lighting voltage, welder ratings, incidental farm service and common use service) are service-qualification and verification terms rather than rates.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-06T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
  }
